course: dictionary
lesson: 6914
title: One short word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word pa has several meanings, so context tells you which one you need. Read the words around it first and ask: is this about family, numbers, weather, school, or a village?
explain: In old stories, children call their parents Ma and Pa, so pa can mean father or dad. It is informal and old-fashioned, so you mostly meet it in old books and some families. «"Ma" and "pa" are among the easiest sounds for babies, so many languages use them for parents», but that does not prove all languages are one family.
explain: Pa is also a unit in science: the pascal, used to measure pressure. Weather maps show it as hPa, hectopascal. Do not mix it up with PA in a school hall, which means a public address system, or with p.a., which means each year.
fact: «Pa» means father or dad, and it is used mostly in old stories and some families.
fact: «p.a.» means per annum, Latin for each year, as in a salary of 30,000 pounds p.a.
fact: «Pa» is the short symbol for pascal, the unit for measuring pressure.
fact: «PA» can mean a personal assistant (a helper at work) or a public address system (loudspeakers).
fact: In New Zealand, a «pa» is a Maori village or hill fort, often with fences and ditches.
exercise: In old stories, children call their parents Ma and Pa. What does Pa mean here? | A unit for measuring pressure | *Father or dad | A helper at work | A small village on a hill
exercise: The weather map shows pressure in hPa. What does the Pa in hPa stand for? | Personal assistant | Hill fort | *Pascal, the unit for measuring pressure | Per annum, each year
exercise: «The salary is 30,000 pounds p.a.» What does p.a. mean? | A public address system | Each week | A Maori village | *Each year, per annum
exercise: The new PA announced the school trip over the loudspeakers. What does PA mean here? | *A public address system, loudspeakers | A hill fort | A personal assistant | A father
exercise: In New Zealand history lessons, a pa was built on a hill with ditches and fences. What is a pa? | A unit for measuring pressure | Pa is an old word for dad | A salary paid each year | *A fortified Maori village or hill fort
test: «Pa, the pressure is rising,» said the weather reporter on the map. What does Pa mean here? | *Pascal, the unit for measuring pressure | Public address system | Maori village | Father
test: «Grandad walked into the kitchen and said, "Pa is home now."» Pa is an informal word. Which meaning fits? | Pressure on a weather map | Each year | A personal assistant | *Father or dad
exam: A weather report says the pressure is 1013 hPa, and a book says «Pa called us in for tea.» How many different meanings of pa do these two sentences show? | *Two: the pascal (pressure) and father (dad) | One, because pa always means dad | None, both are abbreviations | Three: pa, pas and p.a.
